Z||000000||fiero_nightmare||11-02-2001||12:55 PM||||anyone know what other cars have seats that will go in a fiero without heavy mods? <P><BR>my drivers seat is shot so i am going to he salvage yard later and looking for seats.<P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <P>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||11-02-2001||03:28 PM||||Someone recently posted that mid-90's Grand Am seats work and look like the Fiero seats.  You have to swap the Fiero tracks onto the GA seats, but the holes line up - so it's a straight bolt on deal. <P>I'm thinking about getting a pair for daily useage so I can keep my mint seats for shows. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero_nightmare||11-02-2001||05:10 PM||||cool,thanks for the help. i just got home from buying a set of 14 inch 5 spoke finned aluminum wheels with new tires so i am now broke  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  i will have to make another trip to the bone yard to look for seats next month when i have some more money.<P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <P>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw||||reg||7
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-02-2001||05:35 PM||||Try some 3<sup>rd</sup> or 4<sup>th</sup> generation Trans Am/Camaro seats.  Sometimes you can find a pair of power adjustable, leather T/A seats for as low as $150 or so in good condition.  Remember that whatever seat you buy will need to be recovered at some point (unless you own a trailer queen).  Mr. Mikes (my personal seat recovering hero) sells leather seat covers for the T/A seats as well as the Fiero.  Just food for thought.||||reg||1
Z||000004||PBJ||11-02-2001||06:06 PM||||We have Sunfire GT seats with adjustable lumbar support. They bolt right on fiero adjuster.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mickey_Moose||11-02-2001||06:07 PM||||man I wish T/A seats were that cheap up here in Canada - they seem to be more of a hot item here and the price show it. A decent pair of leather seats run for $800+  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>||||reg||1
